# Every text file is LF in the index *and* in the working tree.
#
# `eol=lf` is the part that matters: without it a Windows checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` writes CRLF into the working tree, and since Prettier's
# `endOfLine` default is `lf` it then flags every file it can parse. That made
# `npm run format-check` report ~241 failures locally against CI's 56 — the
# real drift was unfindable in the noise, so nobody ran the check locally and
# the drift reached CI instead. Git still shows no diff for those files (the
# index was always LF), which is why the mismatch stayed invisible.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: no EOL conversion, and no attempt to diff them as text.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.pyc  binary
